        {
          "id": 3331519295,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The problem turned out to be that zooming in or out doesn't affect the splash window on *any* platform. It worked on Fedora 44 if I had captured packets.\n\n(And Kate - KDE, thus Qt - and FeatherPad - Qt, but not KDE - worked if there was text in the window.)\n\nSo not a Qt issue. If we ever decide that zooming the splash window is something we want to do, and do so, it'll probably work correctly on all platforms. Sorry about the fuss....",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
